WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.519
Hey everyone, Quimium is just taking one week off, but we're thrilled to be able to bring you an appearance that Josh made on an incredibly fun podcast called The Puzzler, where the host, AJ Jacobs, tested his puzzle skills with a bunch of original word games.
大家好，Quimium 只需要休息一周，但我们很高兴能为您带来乔希（Josh）在一個非常有趣的播客節目《The Puzzler》中的精彩亮相，节目主持人 AJ·雅各布斯（AJ Jacobs）用一堆原创字谜测试了他的解谜技巧。

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:19.960
As you might know, Josh is a big crossword fan, and it sounds like he had a great time.
正如你可能知道的那样，乔希是个狂热的填字游戏迷，听起来他玩得很开心。

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.600
We thought you might enjoy it too.
我们觉得你也会喜欢。

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.440
While you'll hear our three short episodes they recorded, one after the other.
在节目中，你将会连续听到我们录制的三个短小精悍的片段。

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.359
So take a listen and be sure to subscribe to the puzzler wherever you get your podcasts.
所以请收听，并确保在您获取播客的任何平台上订阅《The Puzzler》。

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:34.640
Hello, puzzlers.
你好，谜题迷们。

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.320
Let's start with a quick puzzle.
让我们从一个简单的谜题开始。

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.759
What do these things have in common?
这些东西有什么共同点？

00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:47.240
Groove recovering, guy losing, bikini stuffing, and dragon training.
寻找律动、失恋男子、比基尼填充和训练飞龙。

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:52.039
That's groove recovering, guy losing, bikini stuffing, and dragon training.
再说一遍，是寻找律动、失恋男子、比基尼填充和训练飞龙。

00:00:52.039 --> 00:01:04.579
The answer and more puzzling goodness after the break.
答案和更多精彩谜题将在广告之后揭晓。

00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:05.579
Hello, puzzlers.
你好，谜题迷们。

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:08.968
back to the puzzler, the simple syrup in your puzzle old-fashioned.
欢迎回到《The Puzzler》，这是你解谜古典鸡尾酒里的糖浆。

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:13.519
I am your host, AJ Jacobs, and I'm here with Chief Puzzle Officer, Greg Flesko, of course.
我是主持人 AJ·雅各布斯，当然，我的身边还有首席解谜官格雷格·弗莱斯科（Greg Flesko）。

00:01:13.519 --> 00:01:15.408
Greg, before Greg, of course.
格雷格，当然，在格雷格之前。

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.340
We asked what do these things have in common?
我们问过，这些东西有什么共同点？

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.749
Groove recovery, guy losing, bikini stuffing, and dragon training.
寻找律动、失恋男子、比基尼填充和训练飞龙。

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.085
The answer might be?
答案可能是？

00:01:24.085 --> 00:01:26.957
Things happening in my apartment right now.
现在正在我公寓里发生的事情。

00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:29.696
Wow, you've got an interesting apartment.
哇，你的公寓真有趣。

00:01:29.696 --> 00:01:30.297
Yeah, no.
好吧，其实不是。

00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:35.308
You know, I had no idea at first and then I went back to groove recovering.
你知道的，一开始我毫无头绪，然后我想到了“寻找律动”。

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:37.579
And I was like, that's very weird.
当时我想，这太奇怪了。

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:41.120
And then I remembered how Stella got her groove back.
然后我想起了电影《怎样重拾律动》（How Stella Got Her Groove Back）。

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:41.882
Exactly.
没错。

00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:50.549
So there's all films that start with how something, how to train your dragon, and the other two.
所以这些都是以“如何（How）”开头的电影，比如《驯龙高手》（How to Train Your Dragon），以及另外两部。

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:52.892
How to lose a guy in 10 days.
《十日拍拖手册》（How to Lose a Guy in 10 Days）。

00:01:52.892 --> 00:01:58.170
And how to stuff a wild bikini, which I think I don't think I've ever heard of that.
还有《如何塞满野性比基尼》（How to Stuff a Wild Bikini），我想我以前可能没听说过这部。

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.615
Annette Punicello, classic.
安妮特·库尼切洛（Annette Funicello），经典之作。

00:02:00.615 --> 00:02:01.430
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:08.389
I bring this up because our guest today started in something else with a how in the title.
我提起这个是因为我们今天的嘉宾曾出演过另一部标题里带有“如何”的作品。

00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:19.110
We are talking about actor, filmmaker, musician, podcaster, and star of the wonderful sitcom Jacob's Family Favorite.
我们要谈论的是演员、电影制作人、音乐人、播客主持人，以及精彩情景喜剧《老爸老妈的浪漫史》（Jacob's Family Favorite）的主演。

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.870
How I Met Your Mother, please welcome Josh Radner.
——是《老爸老妈的浪漫史》（How I Met Your Mother），让我们欢迎乔希·拉德纳（Josh Radner）。

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.159
Hi, it's good to be here with you guys.
嗨，很高兴能和大家在一起。

00:02:26.159 --> 00:02:28.639
We are just delighted.
我们非常高兴。

00:02:28.639 --> 00:02:36.280
And as you know, Josh, you played Ted Mosby on how I met your mother, and you remember that.
如你所知，乔希，你在《老爸老妈的浪漫史》中扮演了泰德·莫斯比（Ted Mosby），你还记得吧。

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.599
That's a good trivia question.
这是一个很好的冷知识问题。

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:40.560
Who did you play?
你扮演的是谁？

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:48.879
And you have a new podcast that you are hosting with series co-creator Craig Thomas called How We Made Your Mother.
你有一个新播客，是你和剧集联合创作者克雷格·托马斯（Craig Thomas）共同主持的，名叫《How We Made Your Mother》。

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:49.960
It's a great podcast.
这是一个很棒的播客。

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.120
I've been listening.
我一直在听。

00:02:52.120 --> 00:03:02.212
And one thing I wanted to ask you right up front, in one of the first couple of episodes, and Craig discuss how I met your mother is a very pussly show.
我想直接问你的一件事是，在前几集中的一手里，你和克雷格讨论了《老爸老妈的浪漫史》是一部非常具有解谜性质的剧集。

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:07.060
Can you talk a little about in what ways is how I met your mother pussly?
你能聊聊《老爸老妈的浪漫史》在哪些方面具有解谜性质吗？

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:07.806
Yeah, sure.
当然可以。

00:03:07.806 --> 00:03:29.736
When I got the show and people would ask me what it was, and I would say, it's almost like if Quentin Tarantino created a sitcom because it would go non-linear and there were, you know, average of 40 to 60 scenes per episode, all kind of scrambled and told out of order, but the central premise of the show is this mystery.
当我刚接拍这部剧时，人们问我这是讲什么的，我会说，这简直就像是昆汀·塔伦蒂诺（Quentin Tarantino）创作的情景喜剧，因为它的叙事是非线性的，你知道的，每集平均有 40 到 60 个场景，全都是打乱顺序、非顺叙讲述的，但这部剧的核心前提是一个谜团。

00:03:29.736 --> 00:03:36.865
You know, I, my character's telling his kids in the year 2030, 2035, I can't remember, I think it's 2030.
你知道的，我的角色在 2030 年、2035 年——我不记得了，好像是 2030 年——向他的孩子们讲述……

00:03:36.865 --> 00:03:47.525
What, you know, the story, the long meandering story of how he met their mother, so they know who the mother is, the audience doesn't know who the mother is.
你知道的，这个故事，那个关于他是如何遇见他们母亲的漫长而曲折的故事，所以他们知道母亲是谁，但观众不知道母亲是谁。

00:03:47.525 --> 00:03:58.660
So the whole thing is structured as this mystery, We know that there's a meeting at some point, but he's gonna take his time and he's gonna fill in all the details.
所以整部剧的结构就像是一个谜团，我们知道他们最终会在某个时刻相遇，但他会不急不慢地把所有的细节都填补完整。

00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:12.699
And sometimes individual episodes are structured as a mystery, I'm thinking of, there's an episode called Ted Mosby Architect that it just looked like Ted was doing all these insane, slightly criminal things.
有时候单集的结构也像是一个谜团，我想起有一集叫《泰德·莫斯比，建筑师》，那一集里泰德看起来在做所有这些疯狂的、稍微有点犯罪倾向的事情。

00:04:12.699 --> 00:04:15.379
And it was confusing, like why was he doing these?
这让人很困惑，比如他为什么要这么做？

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:18.100
And then it's revealed it wasn't actually him.
然后剧情揭晓，那其实根本不是他。

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:27.420
So I think Carter and Craig just had a taste for almost like an elegant withhold of information.
所以我觉得卡特（Carter）和克雷格（Craig）只是有一种爱好，喜欢对信息进行几乎像优雅的克制与保留。

00:04:27.459 --> 00:04:31.180
And there was something very satisfying.
这有一种非常令人满足的感觉。

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:35.899
One of the things we're interrogating in the show is, why has the show maintained its level of popularity?
我们在节目中探讨的问题之一是：为什么这部剧能保持这样的人气水平？

00:04:35.899 --> 00:04:40.019
Why is it minting new fans generation after generation?
为什么它能代复一代地吸引新粉丝？

00:04:40.019 --> 00:04:41.899
Well, I don't know if we can say generation after generation.
嗯，我不知道我们能不能说是代复一代。

00:04:41.899 --> 00:04:52.220
It's been what a lot of years since it went off, but I know a lot, you know, 12-year-old's teenagers, like they're discovering the show, and we're kind of investigating the mystery of the show.
距离它完结已经过去很多年了，但我知道很多，你知道的，12岁的孩子、青少年，他们都在发掘这部剧，我们有点像是在调查这部剧的谜团。

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.139
Why is the show inspired such loyalty and devotion?
为什么这部剧能激发如此高的忠诚度和热爱？

00:04:56.019 --> 00:05:00.939
And I think there's a lot of reasons for that, but one of them I think is it really keeps you on your toes.
我想这有很多原因，但其中之一我认为是它真的让你时刻保持警惕。

00:05:00.939 --> 00:05:03.420
I mean, it asks something of you.
我的意思是，它对你有所要求。

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:11.699
It's not something that, I mean, you can sit back and passively watch it, but it will also engage you in a kind of puzzling, fun way.
它不是那种——我的意思是，你可以靠在椅背上被动观看的节目，但它也会以一种充满谜题的、有趣的方式让你参与进来。

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:13.459
Yeah, well, I love that.
是的，我太喜欢这个了。

00:05:13.459 --> 00:05:17.420
I mean, there's the big puzzle of who the mother is.
我的意思是，这里有一个最大的谜团，那就是母亲到底是谁。

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:21.300
There's the famous episode called The Pineapple Incident.
还有那个著名的剧集，叫《菠萝事件》（The Pineapple Incident）。

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:29.220
He was Ted wakes up next to a pineapple and a woman, played by Danica Keller from The Wonder Years, which is very exciting.
泰德在一颗菠萝和一个女人身边醒来，那个角色由来自《纯真年代》（The Wonder Years）的达尼卡·麦凯拉（Danica McKellar）饰演，这非常令人兴奋。

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:34.180
Oh, and also there was Barney and Ted, we're gonna open a bar called puzzles.
哦，还有巴尼（Barney）和泰德，我们要开一家名叫“谜题（Puzzles）”的酒吧。

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.259
I was gonna bring that up, I love that.
我正要提这个呢，我太喜欢了。

00:05:36.259 --> 00:05:37.100
Oh, you worked her, okay.
哦，你已经说过了，好吧。

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.819
Yeah, that's fantastic.
是的，这太棒了。

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.259
And why is it called puzzles?
为什么叫“谜题”？

00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:43.860
That's the puzzle.
这就是谜题。

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.100
That's the puzzle, that was it, exactly.
这就是谜题，就是这样，完全正确。

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:56.480
And the other crossover is that Ted, the character, is a fan of crosswords.
另一个跨界点是，泰德这个角色是个填字游戏迷。

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:05.180
And there's an episode where you get to meet legendary, friend of the show, friend of our show, Will Shorts, who is a crossword puzzle editor.
有一集里，你遇到了传奇人物、我们节目的老朋友、我们节目的朋友威尔·短兹（Will Shortz），他是一位填字游戏编辑。

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:09.779
Among other luminaries on the, I think, Upper East Side, that episode.
在那一集中，还有上东区的其他一些名流。

00:06:09.779 --> 00:06:20.759
One of the strange things that happens, the longer you're on a long-running show, the writers get to know you and they start thieving a bit.
奇怪的事情之一是，你在一部长寿剧中待的时间越长，编剧们就越了解你，他们开始进行一点“偷窃”。

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:24.360
They start stealing from your life and throwing things into the character.
他们开始从你的生活中偷取素材，并塞进角色里。

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:31.220
So I was a crossword puzzle fan, I remain one, and I would do the crossword puzzle on set.
所以我是个填字游戏迷，现在依然是，我会在片场玩填字游戏。

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:36.639
And sometimes, you know, props would say, do you just want to keep that as your prop for this scene?
有时候，你知道的，道具师会说：“你想直接把这个当成这一场戏的道具吗？”

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:40.759
Yeah, I'm just gonna literally do the puzzle while I'm acting on this.
是的，我就会一边演戏一边真的去玩这个字谜。

00:06:40.759 --> 00:06:42.399
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

00:06:42.399 --> 00:06:43.720
So efficient.
太高效了。

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.160
When Carter is a crossword puzzle guy too.
卡特也是个填字游戏迷。

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:52.839
So it was one of those fun overlaps and then Ted just became a crossword puzzle fan just because I was doing them.
所以这是那种有趣的重合之一，然后泰德就成了填字游戏迷，仅仅因为我在玩。

00:06:52.839 --> 00:06:54.600
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

00:06:54.600 --> 00:07:07.839
And I remember in that episode you talk about, you ask Will about Uli, U-L-E-E, why does that appear so often and you had a theory, which was correct.
我记得在那一集里，你谈到、问了威尔关于“Uli”（拼写作 U-L-E-E）的问题，为什么这个词出现得那么频繁，你当时有一个理论，而且是对的。

00:07:07.839 --> 00:07:08.680
Well, what is it?
嗯，是什么来着？

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.040
Because of the bowels?
因为元音吗？

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.040
Yeah, it's like a huge bowel.
对，它里面有大量的元音。

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.399
And I think it's Eulie's gold is what I've seen it.
我想我见过它是作为《尤利之金》（Ulee's Gold）出现的。

00:07:14.399 --> 00:07:16.519
Greg, is there any other Eulie?
格雷格，还有其他的“Ulie”吗？

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:17.019
Yeah.
对。

00:07:17.019 --> 00:07:18.699
Oh, that's the movie, Eulie's gold.
哦，那是那部电影，《尤利之金》。

00:07:18.439 --> 00:07:18.980
Yeah.
对。

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.519
Yeah.
对。

00:07:20.519 --> 00:07:21.720
Well, that is fantastic.
这太棒了。

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:27.639
I want to talk more about you and puzzles and the puzzle of acting, the puzzle of music.
我想多聊聊你、字谜、表演的谜题，以及音乐的谜题。

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:32.319
But since this is the puzzler, let me do a quick puzzle with you if I could.
但既然这里是《The Puzzler》，如果可以的话，让我和你玩一个快问快答的小字谜吧。

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:39.319
You mentioned the puzzle, the bar that Ted and Barney were going to open called puzzles.
你提到了“Puzzles”，那是泰德和巴尼打算开的一家酒吧的名字。

00:07:39.319 --> 00:07:48.319
Love that, but there's another bar in the show, McLaren's, where they all hung out.
我很喜欢，但剧中还有另一家酒吧，麦克拉伦酒吧（McLaren's），他们经常在那里闲逛。

00:07:48.319 --> 00:07:54.319
So this puzzle is about fictional bars, fictional bars and restaurants and hotels.
这个谜题是关于虚构的酒吧、虚构的酒吧、餐厅和酒店的。

00:07:54.319 --> 00:08:01.946
And the idea is I'm going to read you a fictional Yelp review of these fictional places.
我的想法是，我将读给你们听一份这些虚构地点的虚构 Yelp 评价。

00:08:01.946 --> 00:08:05.759
And then you have to guess what it might be.
然后你们必须猜出它可能是什么地方。

00:08:05.759 --> 00:08:19.560
So, for instance, if I said three stars, I enjoyed a picture of beer at this solid Irish bar on the Upper West Side, warning to women, steer clear of one of the regulars, a red-haired guy in a suit.
所以，举个例子，如果我说三星，我很喜欢在这家位于上西区坚实的爱尔兰酒吧里喝一扎啤酒，警告女性，离其中一个常客远点，一个穿西装的红发家伙。

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.903
He will hit on you relentlessly.
他会没完没了地搭讪你。

00:08:21.903 --> 00:08:23.920
So that would be a clue too.
所以这也是一个线索。

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:41.131
McLaren's Clarence, which is the bar and how I met your mother the red-haired guy, of course is Neil Patrick Harris's character I spent a long time looking at his hair to try to figure this Puzzle of this puzzle is what is the color of Neil's hair?
麦克拉伦酒吧（McLaren's），也就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》里的那个酒吧，那个红发家伙，当然就是尼尔·帕特里克·哈里斯（Neil Patrick Harris）饰演的角色，我花了很长时间看他的头发，试图弄明白这个谜题——这个谜题就是尼尔的头发是什么颜色的？

00:08:41.131 --> 00:08:44.604
I would have them on the ground, but yeah Well, okay.
我本想把它们翻个底朝天，但好吧。

00:08:44.604 --> 00:08:46.636
Yeah, I couldn't figure it out.
好吧，我实在没琢磨出来。

00:08:46.636 --> 00:08:51.944
I didn't know how to describe it, but it's not your average just brown All right.
我不知道该怎么形容，但它绝对不是那种普通寻常的棕色。

00:08:51.944 --> 00:08:54.041
So are you ready for some other?
好了，你们准备好迎接其他的了吗？

00:08:54.041 --> 00:08:56.990
These are not all how I met your mother bars.
这些可不全都是《老爸老妈浪漫史》里的酒吧。

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.340
They could be songs.
它们也可能是歌曲。

00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.083
I think so.
我想是的。

00:08:59.083 --> 00:09:04.149
I can tell you that I get performance anxiety around public puzzle solving.
我可以告诉你，当众解谜会让我产生表演焦虑。

00:09:04.149 --> 00:09:06.784
