00:18:02.779 --> 00:18:10.579
Well, Josh, we are lucky enough to have you come back for more puzzling and more talking about your projects.
乔什，我们很幸运能请你回来，明天继续解谜，继续聊聊你的项目。

00:18:10.579 --> 00:18:20.700
Tomorrow, in the meantime, I do have one extra credit for the folks at home, which is a two-star review.
同时，我给家里的听众准备了一道附加题，这是一个两星评价：

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:27.380
I went to this bar to drink alone quietly, but the regulars would not stop talking to me.
我来到这家酒吧想安安静静地独自喝一杯，但常客们喋喋不休地跟我说话。

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:31.660
One guy writes real estate novels, whatever that means.
有个家伙写房地产生存小说，不管那是什么意思。

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:41.019
Another guy was excited that his name, Davey, rhymes with his job being in the Navy, but the live music's pretty good.
另一个家伙很兴奋，因为他的名字戴维（Davey）和他的工作在海军（Navy）押韵，不过现场音乐还不错。

00:18:41.019 --> 00:18:43.259
So what is that a review of?
所以这是对什么的评价？

00:18:43.259 --> 00:18:45.299
And come back tomorrow for the answer.
明天回来听答案。

00:18:45.299 --> 00:18:50.180
And if you have time in the meantime, check out our feed on Instagram.
如果同时你们有时间，去我们的 Instagram 动态看看。

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:52.140
Hello, puzzlers at Hello, puzzlers.
你好，谜题迷们。

00:18:52.140 --> 00:19:11.019
And we'll see you here tomorrow from where puzzling puzzles that will puzzle you puzzlingly hello, puzzlers.
明天我们在这里见，带来会让你大惑不解的谜题。你好，谜题迷们。

00:19:11.019 --> 00:19:12.480
Let's start with a quick puzzle.
让我们从一个简单的谜题开始。

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:21.599
This puzzle is about canned laughter or audience laughter, which appears in many of our favorite sitcoms, including How I Met Your Mother.
这个谜题关于罐头笑声或观众笑声，它出现在我们许多最喜爱的情景喜剧中，包括《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:19:22.079 --> 00:19:25.799
Now, it turns out canned laughter has a long history.
现在看来，罐头笑声有着悠久的历史。

00:19:25.799 --> 00:19:35.759
In the 1700s, French theater, there were people who were paid to clap.
在18世纪的法国戏剧中，有一些人是花钱来鼓掌的。

00:19:35.759 --> 00:19:38.059
They were called clacks.
他们被称为“鼓掌者”（cliques）。

00:19:38.059 --> 00:19:45.160
That's the name of the folks who were sort of the canned laughter, the live canned laughter from the 1700s.
这就是那些扮演18世纪现场罐头笑声的人的名字。

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:53.032
Now it turns out, when I read the Encyclopedia, I found out that it was a very specialized industry.
现在看来，当我阅读百科全书时，我发现这是一门高度专门化的行业。

00:19:53.032 --> 00:20:04.606
You had the people who clapped, but you had different people doing different ways of supporting the play by pretending to have different reactions.
你有负责鼓掌的人，但你也有不同的人通过假装有不同的反应来以不同的方式支持这部戏。

00:20:04.606 --> 00:20:12.164
So I'm going to give you three words, and you are going to try to guess what those people meant.
所以我将给你三个词，你将试着猜这些人是什么意思。

00:20:12.164 --> 00:20:17.360
Might help if you speak French, but you can always give it a shot.
如果你会说法语可能会有帮助，但你随时可以试一试。

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:24.210
All right, there is the bissures, The commissaires, the commissaires, and the plurices.
好的，有 bissures、commissaires 和 plurices。

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.450
I'm not sure I got this right at all.
我不确定我有没有完全搞对。

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.970
Your French is brilliant though, I'll take it.
不过你的法语很棒，我接受了。

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:35.130
So who were the bissures, who were the commissaires and who were the plurices?
那么 bissures 是谁，commissaires 是谁，plurices 又是谁？

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:48.210
I'll accept even if you get one reaction, I can't even match it up to the word, but just what would people be paid to do when they go to the theater in France in the 18th century?
哪怕你猜对了一种反应，我甚至没法把它和那个词对号入座，我也接受，但只要猜猜18世纪在法国去剧院的人会被付钱做什么？

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:51.049
The answers and more puzzling goodness after the break.
答案和更多益智的好东西，广告之后揭晓。

00:20:51.049 --> 00:20:58.150
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the Hyper-Fixed Podcast.
嗨，我是亚历克斯·戈德曼，播客《Hyper-Fixed》的主持人。

