I am your host, AJ Jacobs.
我是你们的主持人 A·J·雅各布斯。

00:21:47.319 --> 00:21:50.480
I'm here, of course, with Chief Puzzle Officer Greg Pliska.
当然，首席谜题官格雷格·普利斯卡也和我在这里。

00:21:50.480 --> 00:22:01.519
Before the break, Greg, we asked about the specialty paid reactors in 1700s French theater.
休息前，格雷格，我们问过关于18世纪法国戏剧中专门的付费反应人员的问题。

00:22:01.519 --> 00:22:05.960
You had the Clack, which were the clappers, the Reures who laughed.
你有负责鼓掌的 Clack，负责笑的 Reures。

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:09.480
What were the Bissues, the Commissaires, and the Pluruses?
Bissues、Commissaires 和 Pluruses 是什么？

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:14.279
So the Clack is kind of, is that just the clappers, or is that the general term of the whole group?
所以 Clack 是一种，这只是指鼓掌的人，还是整个团体的统称？

00:22:14.279 --> 00:22:17.920
I think that's general, that's the big term, like Bird.
我想那是总称，是个大范围的词，就像 Bird 一样。

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:24.240
I know that word from the opera world, where you also have Clacks, people who cheer for different singers.
我知道这个词来自歌剧界，那里也有 Clacks，即为不同歌手喝彩的人。

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:27.680
Um, I didn't know the sub specialized group.
嗯，我不知道细分的专业群体。

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:30.480
You said basers or bissers.
你刚才说的是 basers 还是 bissers？

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:31.640
B-I-S-S-E-U-R-S.
B-I-S-S-E-U-R-S。
B-I-S-S-E-U-R-S。B-I-S-S-E-U-R-S。

00:22:31.640 --> 00:22:32.480
Okay, okay.
好的，好的。

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:36.119
So, because if you said basers, I would have thought they blow kisses, right?
所以，如果你说的是 basers，我还会以为他们是送飞吻的呢，对吧？

00:22:36.119 --> 00:22:37.880
To best say is the kiss.
因为 baiser 是吻。

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:42.400
But, bees, in the opera world, means again, encore.
但是，bies 在歌剧界的意思是“再来一个”、安可。

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:43.240
Do it again.
再来一次。

00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:47.759
So the bissers must be the people that share encore.
所以“bissers”一定是指那些分享返场（encore）的人。

00:22:47.759 --> 00:22:50.960
Wow, encore to you.
哇，你还返场呢。

00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:51.799
Nicely done.
干得漂亮。

00:22:51.799 --> 00:22:53.720
Okay, one, what are the other two?
好吧，第一个，那另外两个是什么？

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:56.680
All right, what were the common shares?
好吧，那普通股份（common shares）是什么？

00:22:56.680 --> 00:23:00.680
They, it sounds like they arrest the people who don't cheer.
他们……听起来他们会把那些不欢呼的人抓起来。

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:02.079
Yeah, this one is a tough one.
对，这个有点难。

00:23:02.079 --> 00:23:11.079
I would not have thought that this was an entire job, but they are the folks who elbow their neighbors and say, watch this, watch this, this is great.
我本不会想到这是一份完整的工作，但他们就是那种会用胳膊肘碰碰邻居说“看这个，看这个，太棒了”的人。

00:23:11.079 --> 00:23:12.599
That is very specific.
那可真是太具体了。

00:23:12.599 --> 00:23:17.880
I'd like that to, I think just go into random movie theaters and elbow the people next to me.
我希望——我觉得我可以走进随机的电影院，然后用胳膊肘碰碰我旁边的人。

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:19.759
Hey, there's a good scene, isn't it?
嘿，这有个好场景，不是吗？

00:23:19.759 --> 00:23:20.259
Right.
对。

00:23:20.259 --> 00:23:23.372
Well, maybe Josh, he's a filmmaker and he could hire you.
好吧，也许乔什，他是个电影人，他可以雇你。

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:26.059
The last one is Plurisous.
最后一个是 Plurisous。

00:23:26.059 --> 00:23:28.079
You might know this if you know a little French.
如果你懂一点法语，你可能会知道这个。

00:23:28.079 --> 00:23:29.440
Well, wait, wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:32.279
You are P-L-E-U-R.
拼写是 P-L-E-U-R。

00:23:32.279 --> 00:23:34.960
Is it too to cry?
是不是“哭泣”的意思？

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:36.319
It is.
是的。

00:23:36.319 --> 00:23:37.880
These are the weepers.
这些就是哭丧人。

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.240
These are the paid weepers and tragedies.
这些是在悲剧里的职业哭丧人。

00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:45.599
So, which is funny, we have canned laughter, but we don't have canned weeping.
所以，这很有趣，我们有罐头笑声（预录笑声），但我们没有罐头哭声。

00:23:45.599 --> 00:23:47.279
So maybe that's a...
所以也许那是一个……

00:23:47.279 --> 00:23:55.194
And imagine if you got it wrong and you hired some sort of service for your comedy would just be a mess.
想象一下，如果你弄错了，为你喜剧雇了某种哭泣服务，那可就一团糟了。

00:23:55.194 --> 00:23:55.803
Exactly.
没错。

00:23:55.803 --> 00:23:57.934
You have to be very careful.
你必须非常小心。

00:23:57.934 --> 00:24:06.685
Now, I bring all this up because one of our favorite shows has, I guess, reused, and that is how I met your mother.
现在，我提出这一切是因为我们最喜欢的节目之一，我想，被重新使用了，那就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:24:06.685 --> 00:24:22.134
And we are lucky enough to have, as our guest, Josh Radner, who played the main character Ted Mosby, and he is host of a new podcast with series co-creators, Craig Thomas, called How We Made Your Mother.
我们非常幸运地邀请到了我们的嘉宾乔什·拉德纳（Josh Radner），他饰演了主角泰德·莫斯比（Ted Mosby），他与剧集联合主创克雷格·托马斯（Craig Thomas）共同主持了一档新播客，名叫《我们是如何制作你的母亲》（How We Made Your Mother）。

00:24:22.134 --> 00:24:23.200
Welcome, Josh.
欢迎，乔什。

00:24:23.839 --> 00:24:24.339
Hi.
嗨。

00:24:24.339 --> 00:24:29.801
We love the name of your podcast, which is, of course, a play on how I met your mother.
我们很喜欢你们播客的名字，当然，这是对《老爸老妈浪漫史》（How I Met Your Mother）的一个谐音梗。

00:24:29.801 --> 00:24:33.630
It's called How We Made Your Mother, How We Made Your Mother.
它叫《我们是如何制作你的母亲》（How We Made Your Mother）。

00:24:33.630 --> 00:24:41.351
It was that an immediate, like, as soon as you had the idea, like, this is how we're going to do it, or did you go through?
这是一个即兴的想法吗？就像你们一有这个想法，就觉得“这就是我们要做的”，还是经历过一番讨论？

00:24:41.039 --> 00:24:54.790
But it just came to me and I texted Craig and our producer Alec Lev and I said what about how we made your mother and they liked it and we kicked around maybe a couple other different titles.
这个想法突然就蹦出来了，我给克雷格和我们的制作人亚历克·莱夫（Alec Lev）发了短信，我说《我们是如何制作你的母亲》怎么样，他们很喜欢，然后我们又讨论了其他一两个不同的名字。

00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:59.253
But I think we liked something that was, is it homophonically?
但我想我们更喜欢某种……它是同音异义的吗？

00:24:59.253 --> 00:25:00.909
Is that the right word?
那是正确的词吗？

00:25:00.909 --> 00:25:05.300
Something that kind of evoked the original title of the show.
某种能让人联想到节目原名的东西。

00:25:05.300 --> 00:25:08.036
Yeah, I think that's the correct word.
对，我觉得那是正确的词。

00:25:08.036 --> 00:25:09.980
Well, we went even further.
好吧，我们走得更远。

00:25:09.980 --> 00:25:11.996
We went even harder on that.
我们在那方面做得更彻底。

00:25:11.996 --> 00:25:15.235
We liked to come up with ideas for spin-offs.
我们喜欢想出衍生剧的点子。

00:25:15.235 --> 00:25:21.210
And these are, by the way, you are welcome to option any of these from the puzzler.
顺便说一句，这些点子，欢迎你从解谜人（the puzzler）这里买断任何一个。

00:25:21.210 --> 00:25:30.857
And they are all spin-offs where we took out the word met from how I met your mother and replaced it with a word that rhymes with met.
这些都是衍生剧，我们将《老爸老妈浪漫史》（How I Met Your Mother）中的“met”这个词拿掉，换成了一个与“met”押韵的词。

00:25:30.857 --> 00:25:43.239
So for instance, if I said this is a show about the time I wagered $100 on the Super Bowl with your mom, it would be how I bet your mother instead of how I met your mother.
所以，举个例子，如果我说这是一个关于我和你妈在超级碗上赌了100美元的故事，那就是“How I bet your mother”，而不是“How I Met Your Mother”。

00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:51.440
So that is the premise and I'm just gonna go right into my pitches and you can buy them as we go.
所以这就是前提，我直接开始我的推介，你们可以边听边买。

00:25:51.759 --> 00:25:54.559
We're gonna start with the single syllable.
我们从单音节开始。

00:25:54.559 --> 00:25:56.440
So it's like met.
所以就像 met 一样。

00:25:56.440 --> 00:26:01.960
This is a show about doing an extensive background check on your mom.
这是一个关于对你妈妈进行广泛背景调查的节目。

00:26:01.960 --> 00:26:03.240
Oh yes, okay.
哦，是的，好吧。

00:26:03.240 --> 00:26:06.599
So that would be how I vet your mother?
所以那是“How I vet your mother”（我如何审查你的母亲）？

00:26:06.599 --> 00:26:08.740
Exactly, how I vet your mother.
没错，“How I vet your mother”。

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:13.440
How I totally understand your mom's sense of humor.
我如何完全理解你妈妈的幽默感。

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:16.910
How I get your mother.
“How I get your mother”（我如何理解/搞定你的母亲）。

00:26:16.910 --> 00:26:18.470
Exactly.
没错。

00:26:18.470 --> 00:26:23.910
How I stroked your mom's hair in a very platonic G-rated way.
我如何以一种非常柏拉图式的、G级的（老少咸宜的）方式抚摸你妈妈的头发。

00:26:23.910 --> 00:26:28.109
Just don't want to keep that clear for the puzzler audience.
只是想向解谜人的观众澄清这一点。

00:26:28.109 --> 00:26:30.910
How I pet your mother.
“How I pet your mother”（我如何爱抚你的母亲）。

00:26:30.910 --> 00:26:32.910
Exactly.
没错。

00:26:32.910 --> 00:26:35.970
This one is actually a little tricky.
这个其实有点棘手。

00:26:35.970 --> 00:26:54.650
How your mom tries to correct the spelling on my book manuscript but I overrule her yes very good how i said your mother how i said your mother exactly i'm impressed that's a good that's a good crossword not that appears in the crossword now and then.
你妈妈如何试图纠正我书稿上的拼写错误，但我否决了她——是的，非常好，“How I said your mother”（我如何对你母亲说/或某种拼写）——“How I said your mother”，没错，我很佩服，这是一个很好的填字游戏词汇，偶尔会出现在填字游戏中。

00:26:54.650 --> 00:27:02.461
You like every crossword puzzler knows a priest's robe, you know, right We all have an In the closet right here.
你知道的，每个填字游戏解谜人都知道牧师的长袍，你知道的，对吧？我们衣橱里都有一个。

00:27:02.461 --> 00:27:10.900
That's right and we know and what is the one that there's the sumo belt is similar to that But I forget what is that one?
没错，我们知道，还有一个是什么，相扑腰带和那个类似，但我忘了那个是什么了？

00:27:10.900 --> 00:27:16.927
Right, you know or Josh wait Josh looks like you know, oh be no Start that's it.
对，你知道的，或者乔什——等等，乔什看起来你知道，哦，不，Start，就是那个。

00:27:16.927 --> 00:27:18.434
Yeah, I'll be right.
对，Obi（腰带），没准。

00:27:18.434 --> 00:27:20.242
Thank you Japanese belt.
谢谢。日本腰带。

00:27:20.242 --> 00:27:25.818
Oh be is the belt and the boa is another belt-like thing around your neck.
哦，Obi 是腰带，而 Boa 是你脖子上的那种像腰带的东西。

00:27:25.818 --> 00:27:28.756
All right, moving on from that nerdery.
好了，不聊这些书呆子气的话题了。

00:27:28.756 --> 00:27:33.277
I'm gonna go with, now we're bumping it up to two syllables.
我要继续了，现在我们升级到两个音节。

00:27:33.277 --> 00:27:34.332
Two syllables.
两个音节。

00:27:34.332 --> 00:27:40.359
This is a show about being the getaway driver for your mom when she robs a bank.
这是一个关于在你妈妈抢劫银行时做她的逃跑司机的节目。

00:27:40.359 --> 00:27:42.017
How I bet your mother.
“How I bet your mother”（我如何……打赌/或押韵词）。

00:27:42.017 --> 00:27:42.620
